🚀 SIH 26049 – Smart High-Altitude Electronics Protection System

This project is our solution for Smart India Hackathon 2026 – Problem Statement 26049.

The idea is simple: electronic equipment working in high-altitude environments can face extreme cold, low pressure, humidity, vibration, and power-related issues. Instead of waiting for the electronics to fail, we want to **monitor their condition continuously and take action before things get worse**.

Our system uses an **ESP32, multiple sensors, TinyML, automatic thermal protection, and a web dashboard** to monitor the health of the electronics in real time.

The device collects data such as **temperature, humidity, pressure, vibration, voltage, and current**. This data is processed at the edge to understand the current environmental and electronic stress. Based on these values, the system generates a health/risk score and can automatically activate a heater or adjust power usage when required.

The system also sends the collected data to a backend server where it can be viewed through a dashboard. The dashboard gives a clear view of the current health of each unit, sensor values, alerts, trends, and possible problems.

 🔧 What We're Building

* 🌡️ Temperature monitoring
* 💧 Humidity and condensation-risk monitoring
* 🫧 Pressure monitoring
* 📳 Vibration monitoring
* ⚡ Voltage and current monitoring
* 🔥 Automatic heater control
* 🧠 TinyML-based health/risk prediction
* 🔋 Smart power management
* 💾 Local data logging
* 📡 Device-to-server communication
* 🖥️ Real-time monitoring dashboard
* 🚨 Explainable alerts
* 🧬 Digital Twin / What-if simulation

🧠 How It Works

Sensors
   ↓
ESP32
   ↓
Data Processing
   ↓
TinyML / Risk Analysis
   ↓
Health Score
   ↓
┌───────────────┬───────────────┐
│               │               │
Heater       Power Control     Alert
│               │               │
└───────────────┴───────────────┘
                ↓
          Backend Server
                ↓
          Web Dashboard

For example, if the temperature starts dropping quickly while humidity is increasing, the system can identify that the electronics are entering a potentially risky condition. It can then activate thermal protection and notify the user through the dashboard.

🎯 Our Main Goal

We don't want to build just another IoT monitoring system that displays sensor values.

We want the system to **understand the conditions, identify increasing risk, and respond automatically**.

In simple terms:

Sense → Understand → Predict → Protect

This repository contains the hardware, embedded firmware, machine-learning components, backend, dashboard, and simulation work for the project.

This is currently a prototype/proof-of-concept, and the final deployment version would require proper environmental testing and hardware qualification for extreme high-altitude conditions.

